{"results":[{"record_id":"update_2026-08-09__rec_000001","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"no","text_bio_bridge_present":"no","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"yes","primary_exclusion_code":"EC2_no_text_component","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"Primary DNA foundation model paper; the evidence is sequence-only, with single-nucleotide DNA tokenization and masked language modeling. No natural-language text component or text-bio bridge is evidenced.","evidence_snippet":"single-nucleotide tokenization; masked language modeling objective applied to 8,192 bp input sequences"},{"record_id":"update_2026-08-09__rec_000138","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"yes","text_bio_bridge_present":"yes","generative_model_present":"yes","foundation_model_evidence":"yes","primary_exclusion_code":"none","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"Despite using a Qwen3.5-9B backbone, the paper introduces a coordinated multimodal system with EvenClock, a GNN, and a natural-language agent. The biological text interface is central rather than wrapper-only.","evidence_snippet":"natural-language explanations of its outputs; EvenClock encodes two-dimensional spatial coordinates as eighteen clockface sectors of text"},{"record_id":"update_2026-08-09__rec_000227","paper_type":"review_editorial","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"no","text_bio_bridge_present":"no","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"yes","primary_exclusion_code":"review_editorial","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"This is a systematic empirical analysis of existing SCFMs, not a new model contribution. The described models are transcriptome masked-token models, with no natural-language text bridge in the record.","evidence_snippet":"We conduct a systematic empirical analysis of four SCFMs; trained with the same masked-token recipe on transcriptomes"},{"record_id":"update_2026-08-09__rec_000231","paper_type":"unclear","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"no","text_bio_bridge_present":"no","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"EC2_no_text_component","uncertainty_reason":"paper_type_unclear","decision_rationale":"The provided section only shows PubTator3-derived gene relations turned into graphs, so the paper type cannot be resolved confidently. No natural-language text component is evidenced.","evidence_snippet":"Gene regulatory relationships were obtained from the pre-annotated PubTator3 table; treated as undirected graphs in our analysis"},{"record_id":"update_2026-08-09__rec_000082","paper_type":"application_wrapper","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"no","text_bio_bridge_present":"no","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"yes","primary_exclusion_code":"application_wrapper","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"This is a transfer-learning framework around pretrained language-model embeddings for scRNA-seq integration, not a generative multimodal model. The text side is external embeddings, so it is best treated as a wrapper.","evidence_snippet":"combining RNA expression with embeddings from protein language models and general-purpose language models"}]}
